Hi Jake,

Can you confirm you also ran the lines in yellow?
Download the Revolution R Open tarball to a temporary directory and unpack it.
Change directory to the newly created RRO-3.2.2 directory.
Run the following commands to install the rpm file:

> mkdir $HOME/localrpmdb
> rpm --initdb --dbpath $HOME/localrpmdb
> export MY_RPM_DBPATH=$HOME/localrpmdb && \

    rpm --dbpath $MY_RPM_DBPATH --prefix $HOME \

    --nodeps -i RRO-3.2.2.el6.x86_64.rpm

Thanks!

